This product includes data from herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr),
Copyright the herdr authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

- holdspeak/agent_context/rules/{claude,codex,pi,gemini,opencode}.toml are
  herdr v0.9.5's agent detection rules (distribution/agent-detection/),
  copied unchanged under a header that names their origin and license.
- holdspeak/agent_context/screen_rules.py is a fresh Python engine for those
  rules, written after herdr's src/detect/manifest.rs (its regions, its
  contains / regex / line_regex / all / any / not gates and its priority
  order). Our changes: Rust regex syntax is read as Python's (\x{...} and
  \z), the override folder is ~/.config/holdspeak/agent-rules/, rules are
  read from tmux (the pane's visible screen and its title), and no rule is
  fetched from the network.

Nothing is copied from herdr releases before 0.8.0 or from any fork of it
that carries the AGPL.

This product includes ideas and schema shapes from agentring
(https://github.com/mutonby/agentring, read at commit 10b0e55),
Copyright the agentring authors, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. agentring has no NOTICE file of its own.

- No agentring file is copied and no agentring code runs. holdspeak/phone/
  (the event log with seq and replay, the call state machine, pairing by a
  QR token and a device JWT, the signed push payload, the PushProvider
  answers), holdspeak/mcp/families/phone.py (the send_message, get_replies,
  call and status tools) and agent/skills/holdspeak-phone/SKILL.md (the
  etiquette) are fresh code and text written after agentring's relay,
  daemon and skill. Our changes: the hub is the relay (no VPS, no LiveKit,
  no Firebase), APNs in place of FCM, the voice is HoldSpeak's Calls turn
  loop, and the rules to reach the owner are code by control level.
- What each part took, file by file:
  docs/internal/betterment/phone/ABSORBED-FROM-AGENTRING.md.

This product includes ideas from Moonfold
(https://github.com/Mr-Dark-debug/Moonfold), Copyright (c) 2026 T3 Tools Inc.
and Copyright (c) 2026 Moonfold contributors, licensed under the MIT License.

- No Moonfold code is copied. The idea of the provider handoff (an ordered
  fallback list of agents, a limit notice that offers "Continue in ...", a
  deterministic handoff brief built from the thread's history without a
  model, redaction counted by kind, never twice for the same stopped turn,
  allowed providers per project, an optional usage warning) is fresh code in
  holdspeak/services/program_handoff.py, holdspeak/agent_context/usage_limit.py
  and the PG19 parts of holdspeak/services/program_runner.py and
  program_rules.py (docs/internal/betterment/programs/PROGRAMS-DESIGN-2026-10-28.md,
  "PG19 Handoff").

